+// on-screen counter is stamped into the presenter's staging buffer, which is host-visible but
+// deliberately *not* host-cached (see HostBuffer::ensure): it is a write-combined window onto video
+// memory, and reading it back costs an uncached round trip per pixel. A translucent panel over
+// 640x480 blending src-over-dst the obvious way measured ~9.5 ms a frame at --scale 4 -- about
+// 175 ns per pixel, or 22 MB/s, against 16 GB/s for the same buffer written in one memcpy. Passing
